256":"dcf14747aed27f24321ce837c0006d1637c92a818481def3ff5793e2f9aef889","supports":["licenses.code"],"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DeepFundAI/ai-browser/HEAD/LICENSE"}],"id":"github:deepfundai/ai-browser","identifiers":{},"kind":"agent","last_verified_at":"2026-10-18T15:41:31Z","licenses":{"code":{"basis":"repository LICENSE header","declared":"MIT","retrieved_at":"2026-10-18T15:41:39Z","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DeepFundAI/ai-browser/HEAD/LICENSE"},"data":null,"document":null,"weights":null},"links":[{"rel":"primary","url":"https://github.com/DeepFundAI/ai-browser"}],"name":"AI Browser (DeepFundAI)","notes":"The repository holds the Next.js and Electron app: tabs as Electron WebContentsView instances (electron/main/services/tab-manager.ts), scheduling, memory, settings, and the agent wiring in electron/main/services/eko-service.ts. The BrowserAgent and FileAgent themselves are imported from the npm packages @jarvis-agent/core and @jarvis-agent/electron (0.3.x), which the README describes as based on Eko; their npm metadata names FellouAI as author and a placeholder repository URL, and their source is not in this tree. In Deep Explore mode the user confirms or edits the generated workflow, and the agent can ask questions during a run. The README calls it a learning project developed and tested mainly with DeepSeek models. Releases ship macOS and Windows installers.","published_at":null,"relations":[],"review_status":"curated","scope":"core","summary":"Electron desktop browser whose built-in agents, imported from Eko-based npm packages, plan editable multi-step workflows and operate web pages in its own tabs, alongside chat, scheduled tasks and memory.","topics":["web-navigation","workflow","human-in-the-loop"],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://github.com/DeepFundAI/ai-browser"}
